WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.234 line:92%
-Welcome to the show, April.

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.636 size:75% position:38%
-Wow, you have WBAL.
I'm from Baltimore.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:04.304 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-You are from Baltimore.

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:06.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we have our Baltimore
affiliate tonight.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:09.175
That's just a coincidence.
But I'm glad we -- What's this?

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:11.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, my God.
-Happy anniversary.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:13.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You got me a cake!
-I got you a cake.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
-April.
[ Applause ]

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I sure did.
-Oh, my gosh!

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:19.652
-It's special for someone to be
on the fifth anniversary.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:23.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know. And yet John Legend
got me nothing.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:23.656 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I like John Legend.
Leave him alone.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:26.326 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
He may be doing battle for me,
you know.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right. That's true.
-Yeah.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right.
I'm gonna blow it out.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Make a wish.
-All right, okay.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:33.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
-All right.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
And you're here!

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.637 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That was my wish.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:40.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I want to start, April,
by saying,

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
you cover the White House.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:45.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously it became
a very different job

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:47.480 line:92%
after the election, 2016.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
For example, today you were
covering the fact

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:52.719
that the President was tweeting
about Spike Lee

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:53.420 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and calling him racist

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
based on something Spike Lee
said at the Oscars.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:58.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is this beyond your wildest
expectations for where

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
this would be at this point?
-Yes.

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:01.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:04.631
-Any and all things presidential
is what I cover.

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:06.499 line:92%
But I watched the Oscars.

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:08.601 line:92%
I'm an avid viewer of movies.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:09.402 line:92%
I need something mindless

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:12.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
after dealing with
what I deal with every day.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And it's the truth.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.942 line:92%
And I watched "BlacKkKlansman."

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.277 line:92%
I watched Spike Lee's speech.

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:19.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Spike Lee used his script,
or what have you,

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:23.483
his legal pad and paper,
and he spoke about his history.

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:25.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
He spoke about
African-American history.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
He didn't call out
the President.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:31.991
And I'm trying to find where the
President felt it was racist.

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:35.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
And anything the President
tweets, does, says

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:36.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
or is involved in,
that's what we cover.

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:39.432 size:84% position:42%
And unfortunately today
I'm dealing with issues

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:40.700 line:92%
of Spike Lee and the President.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You deal with Sarah Sanders
a lot,

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.204 size:88% position:44%
although probably less
than you would deal with

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:47.674
most press secretaries because
they don't have daily briefings.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:48.942 line:92%
But a few years ago, she tweeted

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:52.378
that she cooked a chocolate
pecan pie for Thanksgiving.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you wrote,
"Show it to us on a table."

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were basically saying that
it was maybe taken out

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:01.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
of a cookbook or a photo of
not a pie she actually cooked.

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:02.956 size:88% position:44% line:92%
But then there was this.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I will say, you know,
I see the world

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:07.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a very different way
than Sarah Sanders.

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:09.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I will say, when I saw
this photo, I liked it.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I thought,
"Well, this is humanity."

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:15.135
At the end of the day, I do want
to see us all getting along.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-So this was a nice moment.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.372
Yet, is it safe to say that
your relationship with her

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
has decayed since
this Thanksgiving moment

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:22.442 size:81% position:41% line:92%
a couple of years ago?

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's decayed like that pie,
yes.

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:29.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:31.384 line:92%
-I'm gonna get in trouble.

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:32.952 line:92%
-You're already in trouble.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is true.
-Yeah.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.589 line:92%
-No, but it's -- it's strained.

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:41.094
You know, I believe in trying
to work with an administration.

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:44.164
There's a thing called friendly
adversarial relationship

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:46.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Mike McCurry,
the first press secretary

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:47.600 line:92%
I ever worked with, said.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.436
He was the press secretary
during the Clinton years.

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:52.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
And at issue is
this press secretary

00:02:52.405 --> 00:02:55.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
who makes personal attacks
in that briefing room.

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:57.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you ask her a legitimate
question

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:59.379 line:92%
that she doesn't want to answer

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:01.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
or she feels like she is
backed in a corner.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:05.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's a sad day when
a reporter who is covered by

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:09.055
the First Amendment cannot
legitimately ask a question

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:09.856 size:84% position:42% line:92%
without being attacked.

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:13.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then once you're attacked,
everyone plasters your face

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:17.597
on certain news organizations
and put targets on your head.

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:20.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So it's a sad day.

